Z||000001||StuGood||08-04-2000||12:02 AM||||Well, maybe it <B>is</B> just a fuse - check them first.<P>This next idea is almost a pure guess, based on practically nothing: Is it possible you have a bad high-blower-speed relay?  I thought there's supposed to be a relay (in the front compartment?) that sends juice directly to the HVAC blower (through a fat purple wire) when you turn the blower knob to "HI."<P>I'm sure at least a few <B>knowledgeable</B> members will chime in any minute now   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ! <BR><p>[This message has been edited by StuGood (edited 08-04-2000).]||||reg||3
Z||000002||My7Fieros||08-04-2000||02:01 AM||||Wish I could help...I know a good bit about the engines, cosmetics, and interior. But anything "electrical" and/or "extras" such as the A/C, I have no idea about! In fact, I got sick of hearing my sickly "ding ding" when the door is open or the lights are on, so I just pulled the little blue box! (That wont cause any probs will it?)...<BR>However, I suspect Stugoods theory sounds good.....  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||7
Z||000003||Indiana_resto_guy||08-04-2000||09:19 AM||||do you mean the high speed blower won't come on? If this is your problem it's the high speed relay located in the trunk up front. Try swaping the plugs on the two relays up there to check it out! Then obtain a new relay if it works!||||reg||6
